### Feature Resources — CRUD
### Modalidad: JWT + RBAC (login como admin)
### Ejecutar en orden: el CREATE guarda el id que usan los siguientes.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
@id = 1

### LOGIN como admin (ejecutar PRIMERO: guarda el token en @token)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### GET ALL — catálogo completo (105 recursos)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### GET ONE
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### CREATE -> 201 (un reporte futuro; el path va en patrón)
# @name crearRecurso
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/api/reportes/ventas-dia",
  "description": "Reporte de ventas del día"
}

### 409 — el par (method, path) ya existe
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/api/pedidos/:id"
}

### 400 — verbo inválido
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "FETCH",
  "path": "/api/reportes/caja"
}

### PATCH — parcial
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos/{{crearRecurso.response.body.$.resource.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Reporte de ventas del día por turno de caja"
}

### DELETE lógico
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos/{{crearRecurso.response.body.$.resource.id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DELETE físico
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos/{{crearRecurso.response.body.$.resource.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
